Description:

JMAP Email/set no longer lets a client move an email out of the scheduled
mailbox by replacing its whole mailboxIds.  Only its EmailSubmission may take
it out, as the patch form of mailboxIds already required.  Previously such a
move succeeded despite the mailbox's mayRemoveItems being false, and the
email's pending send still went out, even after the email was then destroyed.
Moving an email out of the scheduled mailbox never cancels its send: use
EmailSubmission/set with undoStatus "canceled" for that.

Moving an email into or out of the scheduled mailbox other than by an
EmailSubmission now fails with "forbidden" in either form of mailboxIds,
like destroying an email there, rather than "invalidProperties".


